    <h2>Where a Key Actually Comes From</h2>

    <p>A cryptographic key is only as strong as the randomness used to create it. If an attacker can predict or narrow down the possible values a key could take, the key is effectively broken before it is ever used, no matter how strong the encryption algorithm is.</p>

