            <text x="620" y="45" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--text-primary)">Today</text>
            <text x="400" y="115" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--success)">Data A still decrypts under retained key v1</text>
        </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="warning-box">
        <h4><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i> Common Mistake</h4>
        <p>Rotating a key and deleting the old version immediately makes any data encrypted under that old version permanently unreadable. Retained versions must stay available for decryption until every piece of data encrypted under them has been re-encrypted or is no longer needed.</p>
    </div>
</div>
